<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, oil down, meal steady.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, oil down, meal steady.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were down by 100-150 rupees per tonne in central Indian markets as demand from processing plants were limited and arrivals was good. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were down on lack of demand at higher level. Soyoil solvent was down by 200 rupees and soyoil refined was down by 100 rupees per tonne. The undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained steady. Soymeal yellow was $265-267 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for exports. Rapeseed extraction was $97-98 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,300-3,350 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition. The undertone was steady.</p>
